From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Batman <batman@Batman.local>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 23:04:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] browse patch 013: noise AudioBuffer
 getChannelData()/copyFromChannel()
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The other classic browser fingerprinting technique alongside canvas:
render a short signal through an OfflineAudioContext (oscillator +
dynamics compressor is the common recipe), read the samples back via
getChannelData() or copyFromChannel(), hash them. Rendering is
bit-identical across machines sharing the same audio DSP
implementation, so that hash is a stable cross-site tracking id — the
audio equivalent of the canvas fingerprint patches 011/012 already
cover.

Unlike canvas pixels, getChannelData() intentionally returns a LIVE,
writable view onto the AudioBuffer's own storage (mutating it is
spec'd, legitimate behavior for real audio processing) rather than a
snapshot — so noise can't be reapplied on every call the way canvas's
getImageData is, or it would silently drift on repeated reads.
AudioBuffer::EnsureChannelNoised() applies ApplyAudioReadbackNoise()
at most once per channel (tracked via channel_noise_applied_), the
first time either getChannelData() or copyFromChannel() touches that
channel — both call it directly since copyFromChannel() reads
channels_ itself rather than going through getChannelData().

Perturbation is +-2e-7 on ~1 in 8 samples: an order of magnitude below
16-bit PCM's quantization floor and far below any threshold of human
audibility. This exists purely to change the exact float values a
fingerprint script reads, never to be heard or to matter to real
audio processing.

Needed CallWith=ScriptState on both IDL methods to reach the calling
script's origin — AudioBuffer is a plain data container with no
stored ExecutionContext of its own, unlike a canvas element embedded
in a page.

Reuses the PRNG/salt primitives from canvas_noise.{h,cc} (patches
011/012) via a new ApplyAudioReadbackNoise() sharing the file rather
than a third copy of the same splitmix64 generator.

Deliberately scoped to AudioBuffer only. AnalyserNode's frequency-
domain readouts (getFloatFrequencyData/getByteFrequencyData) are
another real but less prevalent audio fingerprint vector, left as a
documented follow-up (docs/ROADMAP.md) rather than folded in here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
